     "page": 1,
     "text": "Cruz Smith and Newman Clinic\nRe: Ronald Ayala (DOB 10/21/1963)\n\nSeptember 13, 2026: Ronald Ayala presented today with complaints of back strain. During the visit, his blood pressure was recorded at 129/96, and his weight was 227 pounds. Mr. Ayala has a known history of Prediabetes/impaired fasting glucose, which is currently being managed with metformin 500 mg. His most recent A1c was 6.4, which we reviewed during the visit.\n\nNovember 07, 2025: Mr. Ayala returned for follow-up on his Prediabetes/impaired fasting glucose. At that time, his blood pressure was 136/86, and he weighed 231 pounds. His A1c had increased slightly to 6.5, but overall, he was doing well. His medication regimen of metformin 500 mg remained unchanged.\n\nDecember 31, 2024: Ronald Ayala visited for an ankle sprain. His blood pressure was 132/92, and he weighed 229 pounds. He continues to manage his Prediabetes/impaired fasting glucose, which is currently under control. A1c at that time was 6.3.\n\nFebruary 24, 2024: Mr. Ayala was seen for follow-up on his Prediabetes/impaired fasting glucose. His blood pressure was 136/92, and his weight 235 pounds. His A1c was 6.6 at the time, but we discussed strategies to bring it back within the target range. He remains on metformin 500 mg.\n\nApril 20, 2023: Ronald Ayala visited for his routine check-up regarding Prediabetes/impaired fasting blood pressure was 127/90, and his weight was 230 pounds. His was 6.2, showing that he is maintaining good control over his blood glucose levels with his current management plan.\n\nAdditionally, Mr. Ayala has a family history of colon cancer, as his mother was diagnosed at age 51 and passed away at age 58. He has been a former smoker, having smoked one pack per day since May 17, 2008, but he quit on July 16, 2024. His disclosure regarding tobacco use has been honest and forthcoming. He also reports consuming approximately four alcoholic drinks per week.\n\nAn outside lab result from Heritage Diagnostic Services dated September 22, 2009, showed a total cholesterol of 251 with an HDL of 63. His fructosamine level was 287, and his nicotine metabolite test was negative. Gamma GT was 41.\n\nDr. Brooke Simpson\nEndocrinology\nCruz Smith and Newman Clinic\n"
    }
